Package: asmtest-desktop
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: 3D assembly execution trace viewer and debugger (GUI)
 asmtest-desktop is a Dear ImGui desktop application for recording, replaying
 and inspecting per-instruction execution traces of hand-written assembly
 routines exercised by the asm-test framework: register/flag/memory state,
 disassembly, live-capture debugging, and a 3D spacetime visualization of the
 recorded execution.
 .
 This package ships the full application, which links the GPL-2.0 Unicorn
 emulator and the BSD-3-Clause Keystone assembler and Capstone disassembler
 engines (all three built from pinned source and vendored privately under
 /usr/lib/asmtest-desktop/, since none is a distro package). Because it
 conveys Unicorn as a binary dynamically linked into the application, the
 built package is effectively GPL-2.0 as a whole even though asm-test's own
 code is MIT. The engines' verbatim license texts are reproduced under
 /usr/share/doc/asmtest-desktop/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES/.
